# 7. The evolutionary frontier makes this much crazier

This is probably the part with the most upside.

## Darwin Gödel Machine

Sakana/UBC's Darwin Gödel Machine does something conceptually very close to where you want to go.

Instead of manually designing one agent forever, DGM maintains an **archive of agent implementations**. Models mutate agent code, candidates are empirically evaluated, successful variants remain available as stepping stones, and the archive branches into multiple lineages rather than greedily keeping one winner. On their reported experiments, the coding agent improved from 20% to 50% on SWE-bench and 14.2% to 30.7% on Polyglot. ([arXiv][7])

This maps beautifully onto your registry.

Instead of:

```text
agentpack/foo
versions:
1
2
3
4
```

you can maintain:

```text
foo-v1
├── foo-v2-verifier
│   ├── foo-v7-parallel-verifier
│   └── foo-v9-memory
│
├── foo-v3-better-tools
│   └── foo-v6-hound-graph
│
└── foo-v4-plan-repair
    └── foo-v8-hierarchical
```

A **phylogenetic tree of agent architectures**.

Now Git history actually isn't enough.

You want:

```text
parent architecture
mutation
benchmark
environment
model
budget
outcome
descendants
```

