# 9. Red Queen Gödel Machine suggests evaluators themselves can evolve

There is already a newer 2026 direction beyond fixed evolutionary objectives.

The Red Queen Gödel Machine co-evolves agents and evaluators rather than assuming one benchmark remains permanently useful. It uses epoch-bound evaluation criteria and reports improvements from adding complementary evaluator signals. ([arXiv][9])

That matters because your registry will eventually hit:

```text
Architecture optimized SWE-bench.
Now everything overfits SWE-bench.
```

You need evaluator diversity.

So your architecture lineage might track:

```text
agent population
       ↕
evaluation population
```

and use:

```text
unit tests
hidden tests
human evaluation
LLM judges
cost
latency
security
reward-hacking checks
```

instead of one leaderboard score.

