# 10. AgentBeats is probably the closest important adjacent project

This one you should study rather than rebuild.

AgentBeats' thesis is that agent evaluation currently requires bespoke benchmark integration, and it standardizes agents and evaluator agents around **A2A for task interaction and MCP for tool access**. Their reported platform field study involved hundreds of judge and subject agents across multiple categories. ([AgentBeats Docs][10])

Their insight is:

```text
traditional:
N agents × M benchmarks
= N*M integrations

standard protocol:
N agents + M benchmarks
```

([AgentBeats][11])

That is exactly what you need.

**Don't invent your own benchmark transport.**

Make your architecture packages export an AgentBeats-compatible subject-agent interface where practical.

Your system becomes:

```text
YOUR PRODUCT
architecture registry
architecture compiler
architecture resolver
architecture evolution
architecture community

       ↓ standardized agent runtime

A2A / MCP

       ↓

AgentBeats
benchmarks/evaluation
```

You can still add your own benchmark infrastructure, but interoperability is valuable.

