# 19. Now Bitsec becomes extremely relevant

Your intuition is correct.

Bitsec already implements a version of:

> **People submit agent designs, validators benchmark them, and the best designs receive economic rewards.**

It is currently a Bittensor subnet. Miners submit security agents, validators run them inside sandboxes against SCA-Bench-style codebases, outputs are scored against human-auditor ground truth, and the submissions/scores/logs are eventually made public after a round. ([Bitsec Documentation][16])

That is extremely close to one part of what you're describing.

But Bitsec is vertical:

```text
security agents
+
security benchmark
```

Your concept is horizontal:

```text
ANY agent architecture
+
ANY benchmark/task distribution
```

